<div class="stonetop-rulebooks">

	<p class="stonetop-rulebooks-lead">
		The books are not ours to hand out, so this system ships none of them. Point it at the
		PDFs you already own and they open in a window here, with the chapter list, the search
		and the books' own page links all working.
	</p>

	<ul class="stonetop-rulebooks-list">
		{{#each rows}}
			<li class="stonetop-rulebook{{#unless this.path}} stonetop-rulebook--unset{{/unless}}">
				<i class="stonetop-rulebook-icon {{this.icon}}"></i>
				<span class="stonetop-rulebook-body">
					<span class="stonetop-rulebook-name">{{this.title}}</span>
					{{#if this.path}}
						{{!-- Tooltipped as well as printed: the row truncates a long path from the
						      end, which is the end that says which FILE it is. --}}
						<span class="stonetop-rulebook-path" data-tooltip="{{this.path}}">{{this.path}}</span>
					{{else}}
						<span class="stonetop-rulebook-note">{{this.hint}}</span>
					{{/if}}
				</span>
				<span class="stonetop-rulebook-actions">
					{{#if this.path}}
						<button type="button" data-action="read" data-book="{{this.book}}"
							data-tooltip="Open this book">
							<i class="fas fa-book-open"></i>
						</button>
					{{/if}}
					{{!-- THE ORDINARY DOOR, and it opens your computer's own file dialog, exactly
					      as Import Book Art does. What happens next is the part that differs: the
					      file is copied into this world so the reader can still fetch it next
					      session (module/books/book-store.js explains why it has to be). --}}
					<button type="button" class="stonetop-rulebook-choose"
						data-action="choose" data-book="{{this.book}}"
						{{#unless ../canStore}}disabled{{/unless}}
						data-tooltip="Choose the PDF on this computer">
						<i class="fas fa-upload"></i>
					</button>
					{{!-- The second door, for a book already on the server: one copied in earlier,
					      or, on a hosted setup, one already sitting in the assets library. --}}
					<button type="button" data-action="browse" data-book="{{this.book}}"
						{{#unless ../canBrowse}}disabled{{/unless}}
						data-tooltip="Pick one already in this world">
						<i class="fas fa-folder-open"></i>
					</button>
					{{#if this.path}}
						<button type="button" data-action="forget" data-book="{{this.book}}"
							data-tooltip="Forget this file">
							<i class="fas fa-xmark"></i>
						</button>
					{{/if}}
				</span>
				{{!-- Hidden, and clicked by the button above it. An <input type="file"> is the only
				      thing that can open the OS dialog, and its selection cannot be handed back to
				      it from script, so it is read in its own change handler and never re-rendered
				      with a value to preserve. --}}
				<input type="file" class="stonetop-rulebook-file" data-book="{{this.book}}"
				       accept="application/pdf,.pdf" hidden>
			</li>
		{{/each}}
	</ul>

	{{#if canStore}}
		<p class="stonetop-rulebooks-note">
			Choosing a book copies it into this world, under
			<span class="stonetop-rulebook-path">{{dir}}</span>, which is what lets the reader
			open it again tomorrow. A book kept there can be fetched by anyone signed in to this
			world who knows its address, so copy one in only if that suits your table.
		</p>
	{{else}}
		<p class="stonetop-rulebooks-note">
			Your account cannot add files to this world, so only a GM can set these.
		</p>
	{{/if}}

	<div class="stonetop-rulebooks-actions">
		<button type="button" class="stonetop-rulebooks-done" data-action="done">
			<i class="fas fa-check"></i> <span>Done</span>
		</button>
	</div>

</div>
